{"lens":{"fp":"4188350394-24634","payload":"{\n  \"score\": 7,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"core/claim/claim.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"message\": \"`zbuild_claim_release` never unsets `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED`, so a second invocation is not a no-op as the design requires.\",\n      \"quote\": \"    # Only release if this process acquired the claim\\n    [[ -z \\\"${_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED:-}\\\" ]] && return 0\\n\\n    # Remove zbuild:claimed (advisory; failures never abort the run)\\n    _ccgl_remove_label \\\"$issue\\\" \\\"zbuild:claimed\\\" || true\\n\\n    return 0\",\n      \"trigger\": \"The design document for this issue states: 'unsets `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED` before calling `_ccgl_remove_label` (advisory). Unsetting first makes a second call a no-op.' Because `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED` is never unset inside the function, any second call that arrives while the variable still holds `\\\"1\\\"` will pass the guard and invoke `_ccgl_remove_label` again on an already-removed label. In production the gh call returns non-zero (label absent), but `|| true` silences it; in the local-fs backend `grep -Fxv` on the already-cleaned file writes an empty replacement and succeeds silently. DSCLA-13 is not affected today because `trap '' TERM` in `_runner_abort_trap` prevents re-entry, but the idempotency guarantee the design chose is absent from the function itself.\",\n      \"introduced\": true,\n      \"fix\": \"code\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh\",\n      \"category\": \"logic\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"message\": \"`claim_coordinator_claim` and `claim_coordinator_release` still use the per-machine label `claimed:<machine>` that the issue required to be replaced with `zbuild:claimed`, and the unit test at lines 44–49 asserts the old label pattern and passes, masking the unimplemented change.\",\n      \"quote\": \"    local our_label=\\\"claimed:${machine}\\\"\",\n      \"trigger\": \"The unit test calls `claim_coordinator_claim \\\"42\\\"` (line 33) and then asserts `grep -q \\\"claimed:\\\" \\\"$labels_file\\\"` (line 45). `claimed:<machine>` is written instead of `zbuild:claimed`. If another run on a different machine checks for `zbuild:claimed` (as `zbuild_claim_acquire` does via `grep -Fxq \\\"zbuild:claimed\\\"`), it will not see the per-machine label and both runs will proceed concurrently — the exact cross-machine collision the issue was designed to prevent (RQLAB-1, RQLAB-2). The corresponding `claim_coordinator_release` removes `claimed:${machine}`, so it also would not remove the `zbuild:claimed` label added by `zbuild_claim_acquire`. The test at lines 44–49 would fail if the function were correctly changed, so it currently passes while enforcing the unfixed state.\",\n      \"introduced\": false,\n      \"fix\": \"code\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/tests/integration/teardown-repeat-signal-test.sh":"10f1f0d17e00b73a37412678d5c4de408cbb2402","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/config/event-schema.json":"30dce672627cb047400df8eb0e095c14e8917247","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"2e2649a7ef6be6c9ab172921cc93401399968c6a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh":"e66946ae97fcf967c5f77ee2ea2518de3b7fda3b","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh":"207c08374724c8c75eb9272e2758d354fb5d5b7b","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"9c5e4918b9c2dd16c79aecbdd522a427e77449b0","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/pipeline/runner.sh":"2b3774255137a68541831d08a7a87f1f84962a5f"}},"scripts/lib/run-status-r